/P 59 0 R
/E (I have seen male clients add an inch or more to their arms by simply focusing on GETTING STRONGER at heavy pulling movements and pressing movements while eliminating isolation exercises all together. I have never seen anyone gain size and muscularity on their arms by doing the opposite. To be clear I am NOT saying you should avoid isolation exercises and only focus on compound ones. All I am saying is to make the compound movements your priorities and throw in 3-5 week heavy strength cycles where you try to get stronger in lifts like chin ups, barbell rows, dips, bench press etc. Add 10-15 kg to these lifts and the high odds are that your arms will grow.)
/Pg 13 0 R
