118 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E (Changing the exercises you do is very important, but what is more important is to change your rep range. Most rep ranges have muscle building value but training in each of them is an entirely different experience. Try comparing sets of squats for 20 reps to sets of squats for 2 reps. VERY different yet both rep ranges build muscle.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
119 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E (The main muscle building rep ranges can be broken down into three categories: LOW reps \(1-5 reps\),MODERATE REPS \(8-12 reps\) and HIGH REPS \(15-20 reps\). Each of them has been PROVEN to build muscle.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
120 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E (The low rep ranges are excellent for building maximal grinding strength. Its also been observed that the low rep ranges build hard and dense looking muscle. I once had a client that competed as a high-level physique competitor and he almost never utilized low reps. Once I convinced him to do some heavy low rep strength training his physique took on a whole new look. He added lbs of hard and dense muscle and became a convert. Now he regularly cycles in periods of low rep training.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
